if you were to describe halos  traditional multiplayer as a house party  a small gathering of friends and  strangers for an evening of laughs and  heroics inhaler fight a new war zone  mode is more like a festival you are  still surrounded by the same sights and  sounds and halo signature style of  combat is as unmistakable as ever put on  war zone you are free to choose where to  spend your time and where to concentrate  your fire power right now you're looking  at the world first reveal of the raid on  apex 7 level in one section of this  sprawling open world map you could for  example be busy mowing down hordes of  Covenant AI on the opposite side of the  island you might find teammates  assembling a warthog gearing up for some  four-player drive-bys in one of the  command posts you could find a three-way  skirmish between both human teams and  the AI and on another you might  encounter a legendary elite boss  patrolling the area waiting for someone  foolish enough to cross its path how all  these different attractions come  together under single gold is what makes  war zone the most unique and interesting  addition to the Halo series in years the  overarching objective is for your team  of 12 Spartans to accumulate a thousand  points before your opponents do how this  is done is your choice you can for  example and a single point by killing  someone on the opposing team or you  could triple in a stream of points by  controlling one of the maps basis or you  could add 25 points for taking out an  elite a I or if you manage to kill a  legendary boss you can earn a  game-changing a hundred and fifty points  a single game of war zone can typically  last up to 30 minutes teams frantically  try to cross the finish line but there's  also a backdoor path to victory each war  zone map features three bases the  players can occupy a patine manages to  control all three bases at the same time  their opposing teams based core is then  exposed if that teams core is destroyed  regardless of what score they have  lose the match it means that you can  still snatch victory from the jaws of  defeat even if lagging behind by 700  points how these gameplay goals clash  and trip into one another makes war zone  particularly chaotic and unpredictable  at times here you can see me fighting to  covenant elders these hulking AI pose  with devastating melee attacks  overcoming them demands high levels of  concentration and here just as I got  into the right rhythm suddenly I was  attacked while you're posing team plans  had to be abandoned it's a degree of  fluctuation the tremendous sense of war  at scale and the sheer breadth of  options that makes war zone such an  exciting prospect all this may suggest  war zone is prohibitively complex but  it's actually accommodating for all  kinds of players especially casual your  spawn points are well protected and  those who aren't particularly skilled  can if they wish just concentrate on  taking down AI these players can add to  the final score as much as the killed  streaking veterans can in fact everyone  can bring something to war zone those  who aren't the most skilled marksman can  charge up score tallies just by  occupying basis even the thrill seekers  who want to leap onto Covenant ghosts  madly stick a grenade on the engine and  dash away just before the bomb goes off  are still in their own mad little way  adding to the total score seasoned  veterans of course will want to be doing  all these things Microsoft wants war  zone to a massive vast community of  players not split apart the way halo 4  said being after the premium DLC arrived  which is why war zones 50 maps will be  free however in place of the DLC is  micro transactions which allows players  to buy more powerful and exotic vehicles  and weapons so a couple of caveats first  you can still earn currency by grinding  second each weapon essentially has a  manner school which in Halo is called a  wreck  clever each warzone game starts at rec  level one and only in the late game can  players start using the most powerful  weapons they have purchased it's not  quite pay to win but casual players with  cash to burn will have an undeniable  advantage over casual have-nots whether  that advantage will extend over to the  hardcore players however remains to be  seen microtransaction worries aside  warzone could very well be the most  interesting thing to happen to Halo and  indeed multiplayer shooters for quite  some time it comes bundled with halo 5  guardians which ships worldwide on a  favor 27 stay tuned to gamespot for the  review  you
 

